[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-10260"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059427/assets/5117030d23370b2167513b7a2eee5258aae4eb9f45ad428fd82e4334c4ce6638.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1+3t,\\,y=2{t}^{3/2},\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2})=3{t}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{(3{t}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9+9t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+t)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\cdot {\\frac{2}{3}(1+t)^{3/2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{8}-2 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178/selection/92754e33e0ca3179f8830ccc9d31117e683483f0d0561f2ccc08d3669e74d889" :answer/id #uuid "8d619fca-f90d-5146-9be3-71804e5e68c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178/selection/372d1516d28a34fec153af7e3f79c55a812b0e3eb0e76b19bcd6c9b14b09c206" :answer/id #uuid "7d4ba437-3c22-5035-a06b-81a306e49bca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178/selection/6732318ae31777557413875c2bfab1df5911db6b432215cc29f736de6d1e75b2" :answer/id #uuid "fac1f9cd-ec8f-532e-a5bf-d126e96ff060" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178/selection/5ce5738ebf6d1d9f9a94e838ac9b535b878d4e1a8c2b5c97281814e84c17c502" :answer/id #uuid "b8d10aa3-f972-5374-98a9-aee16a124368" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178/selection/6d64004f0f279535da737fd2b6d0a28296f3aed4bda0818d662cfb60721153b2" :answer/id #uuid "f4e5fe5b-59f6-5247-b4f4-fe90049360ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce576d09-0f0d-5640-9cbb-4e47252b3ef7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15178/selection/6732318ae31777557413875c2bfab1df5911db6b432215cc29f736de6d1e75b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-15178/selection/92754e33e0ca3179f8830ccc9d31117e683483f0d0561f2ccc08d3669e74d889" "q-15178/selection/372d1516d28a34fec153af7e3f79c55a812b0e3eb0e76b19bcd6c9b14b09c206" "q-15178/selection/6732318ae31777557413875c2bfab1df5911db6b432215cc29f736de6d1e75b2" "q-15178/selection/5ce5738ebf6d1d9f9a94e838ac9b535b878d4e1a8c2b5c97281814e84c17c502" "q-15178/selection/6d64004f0f279535da737fd2b6d0a28296f3aed4bda0818d662cfb60721153b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15178" :question/id #uuid "9a2f2890-829e-5660-aa0e-71dea52c1f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-15178" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059427/assets/ca290e8fd51edddf4381ec267b8e0a5692d0e52bd2a36b7d43ab89cbeb5cf00d.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebd2a5c8-5d15-589d-81c9-9b67f4e8f0b3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" :answer/id #uuid "f0c577fb-691d-57fd-ab02-f70a3a9b2a67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907/selection/8b0da25323387be7cd3dda381ee4e2ebbdc8b10be241bc2e3eeead0da24f888a" :answer/id #uuid "ac5203e7-295c-5cde-ade8-7bdc57017df7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "e54eefaf-5718-5727-b1e7-00b051a3a154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "fe4d8ca0-be6d-56ac-86ac-23faa6a962da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "eb1279d0-877a-5f5a-9885-6f66c080cbe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da5aa7ec-dabe-5539-bb7e-9025da25e2b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20907/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer-field/choices ["q-20907/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" "q-20907/selection/8b0da25323387be7cd3dda381ee4e2ebbdc8b10be241bc2e3eeead0da24f888a" "q-20907/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" "q-20907/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-20907/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20907" :question/id #uuid "fb9131cb-db34-55f4-9b8c-bfeb56041029" :question/math-academy-id "q-20907" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+5,\\,y=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1),\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+5))=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-20907/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c82bbc8-83bc-55f8-be32-4d63f6db7261"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027/selection/3d21b06e853b67d14326e86db991591505276fb67291f1bbd77f6af0a6820326" :answer/id #uuid "630de36d-f891-5720-994c-cd5ca01b5ea5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027/selection/de4d4f7b1cf0c14744894693f1a88c8e780c838a6ec5cbd759ede5633d3db056" :answer/id #uuid "df6b4862-9700-52d8-9959-e7bfa365aadb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+8}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027/selection/ec1fc5b200685ec9c04fd804c58dda5ca7b751670354c9bad4ee32011abba26f" :answer/id #uuid "57bc87d9-25f4-5fe2-a09d-9912b39de6bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{10{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027/selection/ab313074e7131593d770cf20552dc1875f23d67def7655b77be04586c174685b" :answer/id #uuid "2c8dced7-0d7e-5362-8950-dd402b3b6dd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027/selection/02a712f50b68587e6da3d0e583acc9280edcb8d46df8121d35cb2158daf58aa9" :answer/id #uuid "df23ba4c-322f-5fc7-b35c-62614b410f0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5{sin}^{2}⁡t-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+32}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "686fe979-0d5e-5bdb-975a-3702e1512152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123027/selection/ec1fc5b200685ec9c04fd804c58dda5ca7b751670354c9bad4ee32011abba26f" :answer-field/choices ["q-123027/selection/3d21b06e853b67d14326e86db991591505276fb67291f1bbd77f6af0a6820326" "q-123027/selection/de4d4f7b1cf0c14744894693f1a88c8e780c838a6ec5cbd759ede5633d3db056" "q-123027/selection/ec1fc5b200685ec9c04fd804c58dda5ca7b751670354c9bad4ee32011abba26f" "q-123027/selection/ab313074e7131593d770cf20552dc1875f23d67def7655b77be04586c174685b" "q-123027/selection/02a712f50b68587e6da3d0e583acc9280edcb8d46df8121d35cb2158daf58aa9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123027" :question/id #uuid "a37e6009-e864-56bc-93ae-b166a2b05514" :question/math-academy-id "q-123027" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=8t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$ ?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=8-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(8-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+64-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{10{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123027/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebd2a5c8-5d15-589d-81c9-9b67f4e8f0b3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348088/field-1/64e30c82eef5691561bfd250c52f7857cc523ff8c5ca0a30cd86d8eec79a1471" :answer/id #uuid "f21b4205-fe95-5d61-aa2e-072832d7192a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348088/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "42de287f-50e0-5642-9370-c74cd9501015" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348088/field-1/64e30c82eef5691561bfd250c52f7857cc523ff8c5ca0a30cd86d8eec79a1471" :answer-field/choices ["q-348088/field-1/64e30c82eef5691561bfd250c52f7857cc523ff8c5ca0a30cd86d8eec79a1471"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348088" :question/id #uuid "49cd7d08-c239-5b6f-9d68-7ee1350ff2ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-348088" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059427/assets/be9e314ed11882842bbf9a74deeb3a994596c8275a4e854ffc66327fa0008058.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =2{\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-348088/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c82bbc8-83bc-55f8-be32-4d63f6db7261"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348088"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
